# Held Rust ordinary geometry factual checker

Source only. No actual Rust geometry output has been read by this author, and no checker, target, formatter or publisher was executed. Root supplies closed runtime operands after the genuine Native release and reviewed final ten-path workflow. The unsealed draft is documentation and cannot satisfy the runtime authority gate.

Invoke the reviewed physical `check.py` with `--custody PATH#SHA --outer-execution PATH#SHA --Root-artifact-acceptance PATH#SHA --workflow-source-preparation PATH#SHA --output-dir FRESH_IGNORED_DIRECTORY`. All actual operands are authenticated in full. The final workflow must use the accepted owner02 and observer02, exact shared custody and quality constants, and its own fully authenticated apply/validate Sources. Only the read-only workflow `application()` metadata/archive validator is called. No workflow main/target/format/build operation is invoked.

The checker requires the real current full Source membership and all archives, ten exact literal/formatter correspondences, protected dispatcher owners, actual runtime3+28 bindings, four role-specific quality argv, derived full test summaries and exact two existing ignored names, sole genuine Cargo artifact, immediate recorder executable SHA, raw DOS/COFF/optional/section headers, sixteen directories, entry and .text membership, and the actual 8 MiB/4096-byte stack reserve/commit. Root's artifact approval must bind the same build/Source/executable and carry its agreed schema and accepted/no-gates flags.

The complete argc3 input request, original IDF/converted epJSON/actual input-only conversion and all Raw families/order/values are retained and joined. Typed names, actual IDs, vector order, Zone-space-Surface-Construction links, literal vertices and input selectors are checked without ID offsets or geometry equations. Every scalar DTO is checked against its own bits/class/value; every selected returned owner and diagnostic shape is retained. Caller before/after report registry allocations and full tails, named indices, table, Scan, backend counters and complete byte-prefix witnesses are checked. Actual Err/unreached results remain errors/unavailable and are never assigned parity or PASS.

The outer stdout includes the recorder's Source-defined final 8000-byte decoded tails of both actual child logs, then the recorder receipt row and workflow custody row. The checker authenticates the full prefix and both records; it never treats the full log as one JSON record or drops the output tail. All actual stdio bytes are independently hashed. Current inputs, binaries, Sources and all seen artifacts are rehashed before writing a fresh ignored review.

Only comparer02 `snapshot`, `conversion` and `decode_raw` helpers are reused. `authenticate`, `joins`, `compare`, `selected` and Native result readers are not called. Native release metadata may be authenticated by the reviewed workflow application validator; no Native geometry numerical payload is read. No expected Rust geometry or formula output is supplied. Factual `accepted:true` means custody/shape/input facts passed, with the actual initializer outcome retained. It does not mean the initializer returned, geometry matches Native, or an ordinary gate passed.
